      "name": "Cardiovascular Compromise and Hemodynamic Instability",
      "description": "Cardiovascular collapse due to hypoperfusion, shock, or cardiac failure results in inadequate blood pressure and perfusion to vital organs. Key features include ABP, HR, CVP, and signs of shock or heart failure. Such instability often precipitates multi-organ failure and increases mortality.",
